# Confluence Guarded Crawler — Access & Instance Settings (`access_settings.env`)
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dedicated to: confluence-wiki-crawler
# (Note: *.env files are gitignored so your instance URL, token, identity,
#  and space lists are never committed to GitHub. Copy `access_settings.env.example`
#  to `access_settings.env` and fill in your values below.)
#
# 1. CONFLUENCE_BASE_URL:
#    Base URL of your Atlassian Confluence Data Center / Server instance
#    (e.g. https://wiki.example.org)
#
# 2. CONFLUENCE_CRAWLER_API_KEY:
#    Personal Access Token (PAT) for the crawler account
#
# 3. CONFLUENCE_CRAWLER_USERNAME & CONFLUENCE_CRAWLER_NAME:
#    - CONFLUENCE_CRAWLER_USERNAME : Crawler's short login/account username
#                                    (stored in history.createdBy.username and /display/~<username>)
#    - CONFLUENCE_CRAWLER_NAME     : Crawler's full Confluence displayName
#                                    (stored in history.createdBy.displayName and rendered @mentions)
#    Setting BOTH enables strict three-way identity & ownership verification
#    (live token `whoami` == .env identity == content `history.createdBy`).
#
# 4. PERMISSION TIERS (Where the crawler is ALLOWED to read vs. write):
#    - CONFLUENCE_ELEVATED_ACCESS_SPACES:
#      Comma-separated list of space keys where the crawler has ELEVATED ACCESS
#      (read-only pages + create/edit/delete own blogposts + add comments/replies
#      + edit own comments + delete own/mentioned comments + like/unlike).
#
#    - CONFLUENCE_READONLY_SPACES:
#      Comma-separated list of space keys (or `*` for all other server-accessible spaces)
#      where the script enforces STRICT READ-ONLY access (reading/searching/crawling
#      pages, comments, and attachments is allowed, but ALL writes—blogposts,
#      comments, replies, likes, edits, deletes—are blocked by the script even if
#      the server would allow them). Takes precedence over elevated access if a
#      space is listed in both.
#
# 5. INITIAL SEARCH & STARTING SCOPE (Where the crawler looks FIRST to limit server load):
#    - CONFLUENCE_DEFAULT_PAGE (Optional Recommended Starting Page(s)):
#      One or more comma-separated page URLs, `/x/...` tiny links, or numeric page IDs
#      where the crawler should start first (accessible via `get-page --default`,
#      `crawl --default`, and `search --default-pages-only`). If left empty, falls back
#      to the homepage of the first space in `CONFLUENCE_DEFAULT_SPACES` (or
#      `CONFLUENCE_ELEVATED_ACCESS_SPACES`).
#
#    - CONFLUENCE_DEFAULT_SPACES (Optional Default Space(s) for Initial Searches):
#      Comma-separated list of space keys searched by default when `search`,
#      `recent-edits`, or `find-mentions` is run without `--all-spaces` (`--wider`)
#      or `--space <KEY>`. If left empty, automatically defaults to
#      `CONFLUENCE_ELEVATED_ACCESS_SPACES`.
#
# 6. SERVER LOAD PROTECTION (Optional):
#    - CONFLUENCE_THROTTLE_MS:
#      Minimum polite delay in milliseconds between consecutive HTTP requests
#      (default: 0; can also be passed per command via `--throttle-ms <MS>`).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFLUENCE_BASE_URL=PASTE_YOUR_CONFLUENCE_BASE_URL_HERE
CONFLUENCE_CRAWLER_API_KEY=PASTE_YOUR_CRAWLER_CONFLUENCE_PAT_HERE
CONFLUENCE_CRAWLER_USERNAME=PASTE_YOUR_CRAWLER_USERNAME_HERE
CONFLUENCE_CRAWLER_NAME=PASTE_YOUR_CRAWLER_DISPLAY_NAME_HERE
CONFLUENCE_ELEVATED_ACCESS_SPACES=PASTE_COMMA_SEPARATED_ELEVATED_SPACE_KEYS_HERE
CONFLUENCE_READONLY_SPACES=
CONFLUENCE_DEFAULT_PAGE=
CONFLUENCE_DEFAULT_SPACES=
CONFLUENCE_THROTTLE_MS=0
